    metaTitle: 'Trademark vs Trade Name — Key Difference Explained for Indian Businesses',
    metaDesc: 'A trade name is what you register with MCA to operate as a company. A trademark is the IP right that protects your brand exclusively. Both are needed for full protection.',
    quickAnswer: "A trade name (or company name) is the name registered with MCA under which your business legally operates. A trademark is the exclusive IP right registered with IP India that prevents anyone else from using your brand name. Company registration does NOT give you trademark rights — you need both.",
